  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When using a personal mirror, I like to toggle \"grabbable\" to always be able to shift it around. HOWEVER, a huge inconvenience, and annoyance, is that when I reach for any highlighted object in front of it, like an item in the world, or pencil to write with, it also grabs the mirror behind it. If the mirror is larger, it can be very annoying to move it completely out of the way, grab the object, if you're lucky enough to, only for it to happen again once you place it down.\nFor example, please try to use a pencil with a grabbable personal mirror in front of you, and the whole mirror will literally fly around with the pencil while you write, as if you're holding two objects in your hand. Not a good experience.\nThe best thing here would be for the game to know whether or not I am trying to interact with the mirror based on if another object is highlighted with that hand.\nBottom line, if there is a grabbable object in front of the personal mirror, even though grabbable is enabled, I do not want to grab the mirror. I do not want to dig into my action menu just to change it for that one moment, either. Thank you for your time and consideration.",
